<title>SOUTH AFRICA: TABLE - Bowler H1 share, div rises.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Bowler H1 share, div rises.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended June 30</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, (cts)		4.09	  vs 3.38</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 1.35	  vs 1.17</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   3.50	  vs 2.90</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   5.11	  vs 4.24</p>
<p>    Tax			 1.61	  vs 1.34</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   1.32	  vs 1.54</p>
<p>    Turnover		  26.89	 vs 21.62</p>
<p>Div payable Aug 27</p>
<p>on register Aug 22</p>
<p>Full name: Bowler Metcalf Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Directors said that all divisions in the packaging group were  operating on budget and that there was no reason this should not be  maintained until year end. They said the firm was currently targeting  its injection-blow and tube divisions for further development. Its  wholly-owned subsidiary, Bowler PET (Pty) Ltd, would occupy a new  2,500 square metre factory as scheduled in August.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
